{"created": "2026-03-17T23:26:09.555533+00:00", "modified": "2026-03-17T23:26:10.186425+00:00", "id": 19077748, "conceptrecid": "14590061", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19077748", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.14590061", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19077748", "metadata": {"title": "3D models of the human scapula and humerus with defined anatomic landmarks", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19077748", "publication_date": "2026-03-17", "description": "<p>This repository contains 3D models of the human scapula and humerus (*.stl) derived from computed tomography (CT) scans, with spreadsheets (*.csv) detailing demographics and spatial coordinates of a limited set of anatomic landmarks. The models were taken from a convenience sample and include data from over 400 shoulders, with a mix of healthy and pathologic bones from individual and paired anatomies.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>v1.1 expands the contents of the prior release to now include a total of:<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; 275 shoulders, including paired scapulae and humeri<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; 125 complete humeri<br>-&nbsp; &nbsp; 25 complete scapulae<br>- &nbsp; &nbsp;Additional parameters are reported for existing and new models: Radii of the glenoid circle, humeral shaft, and humeral head</p>\n<p>v1.11 corrects body weight in the paired humeri spreadsheet (incorrectly reported in 'lb' but labeled 'kg' originally, corrected to kg)</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Henninger, Heath B.", "affiliation": "University of Utah", "orcid": "0000-0002-3635-1289"}], "contributors": [{"name": "Chalmers, Peter N.", "affiliation": null, "type": "DataCollector"}, {"name": "Jacxsens, Matthijs", "affiliation": null, "type": "DataCollector"}, {"name": "Kawakami, Jun", "affiliation": null, "type": "DataCollector"}, {"name": "Kolz, Christopher W.", "affiliation": null, "type": "DataCollector"}, {"name": "Sulkar, Hema J.", "affiliation": null, "type": "DataCollector"}, {"name": "Suter, Thomas", "affiliation": null, "type": "DataCollector"